    "title": "Oscars 2026 Winners List: ‘One Battle After Another,’ ‘Sinners’ and More",
    "text": "AdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENTOscars 2026 Winners: The Complete ListThe winning actors, directors, pictures and more at the 98th annual Academy Awards.Paul Thomas Anderson, at microphone, accepts the best picture Oscar for “One Battle After Another.”Credit...Philip Cheung for The New York TimesPublished March 15, 2026Updated March 17, 2026Oscars 2026: Read highlights of the 98th Academy Awards.The movie awards season finally came to a close Sunday night, with the 98th edition of the Academy Awards, which took place at the Dolby Theater in Hollywood.“One Battle After Another,” which was nominated for 13 awards, received the highest honor of the night: best picture. Paul Thomas Anderson won for best director and Sean Penn, though he wasn’t in attendance, received the best supporting actor award. The film also won in the newly added category, best casting (Cassandra Kulukundis).With a record-breaking 16 nominations, “Sinners” took home four awards. Its writer-director Ryan Coogler won best original screenplay, and its star, Michael B. Jordan received best actor.Conan O’Brien hosted the show with a slew of gags about the future of A.I., while a heartfelt in memoriam segment honored Rob and Michelle Reiner, Robert Redford, Diane Keaton, Catherine O’Hara and others.See below for a full list of winners.Best Picture“One Battle After Another”Read our review.Nominees in this category: “Bugonia”; “F1”; “Frankenstein”; “Hamnet”; “Marty Supreme”; “The Secret Agent”; “Sentimental Value”; “Sinners”; “Train Dreams”ImagePaul Thomas Anderson on the Oscars stage.Credit...Philip Cheung for The New York TimesA correction was made onMarch 17, 2026: An earlier version of this article omitted the name of one nominee from the best original song category. Diane Warren was nominated for “Dear Me” (“Diane Warren: Relentless”).Shivani Gonzalez is a news assistant at The Times who writes a weekly TV column and contributes to a variety of sections.A version of this article appears in print on March 17, 2026, Section C, Page 5 of the New York edition with the headline: Oscars 2026 Winners: The Complete List. Order Reprints | Today’s Paper | SubscribeAdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENT",
